//@version=6
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                            F V G   T R A D E   E N T R I E S
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  Indicator Name : FVG Trade Entries
//  Author         : Forex_Market_Insights
//  Version        : v6.0 — July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
//  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
//  │  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N                          │
//  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//  I am Forex_Market_Insights, the publisher and sole original author of this exact
//  implementation of "FVG Trade Entries." I designed the structure of this tool, wrote every
//  line of the Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple asset
//  classes and timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the three-candle Fair Value Gap detection
//  routine and its confirmation gating; the ATR-relative minimum-gap size filter; the object
//  based zone registry that tracks every unmitigated gap; the first-tap detection and per-zone
//  single-fire locking that prevents duplicate signals; the optional higher-timeframe trend
//  gate; the entry resolution model with selectable zone-edge and equilibrium modes; the ATR
//  buffered invalidation engine; the risk-multiple target ladder producing four take-profit
//  levels; the complete visual system of zones, risk and reward regions, level lines, right
//  anchored labels and the diagonal trade projection; the live trade-state tracker that extends
//  a setup until it resolves and then freezes it; and the alert framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.0, July 2026). Any
//  future modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
//  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
//  │  O R I G I N A L   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N                            │
//  │  V E R I F I C A T I O N   &   D E C L A R A T I O N                                    │
//  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Forex_Market_Insights. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected
//  or open-source script. No third-party library, no republished open-source script and no
//  re-skinned built-in indicator forms any part of this work.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying trading CONCEPTS used here are publicly documented
//  and widely taught in the trading community: the Fair Value Gap / three-candle imbalance, the
//  idea of price returning to rebalance an inefficiency, invalidation placed beyond a zone's far
//  edge, and targets expressed as multiples of initial risk. These concepts are public knowledge
//  and belong to no single author. My original contribution — and what this declaration covers —
//  is the specific CODE IMPLEMENTATION of those concepts: my own formulas, my own data
//  structures, my own state-management architecture, my own filtering and locking logic, and my
//  own visual and alert design. Conceptual overlap with other tools that also discuss Fair Value
//  Gaps is therefore unavoidable and expected, but there is no source-code overlap of any kind.
//
//  Standard Pine Script built-in functions (ta.atr, ta.ema, request.security, and the drawing
//  primitives box / line / label) are used only as low-level language facilities inside my own
//  engine, in the same way any developer uses a programming language's standard library.
//
//  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
//  │  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S                                        │
//  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//  1) FAIR VALUE GAP DETECTION
//     A bullish FVG is registered when the current bar's low sits entirely above the high from
//     two bars back, leaving an unfilled window of price that no trading occurred in. A bearish
//     FVG is the mirror: the current high sits entirely below the low from two bars back. Each
//     confirmed gap is drawn as a semi-transparent zone and stored in a live registry.
//
//  2) NOISE FILTERING
//     Every gap is measured against current ATR. Gaps smaller than the configured ATR multiple
//     are ignored entirely, so micro-imbalances on fast charts never clutter the workspace or
//     produce low-quality setups. An optional higher-timeframe EMA gate restricts setups to the
//     prevailing higher-timeframe direction.
//
//  3) TAP-BASED SETUP TRIGGER
//     A setup is generated only when price returns and taps an unmitigated zone — a long when
//     price trades back down into a bullish gap, a short when price trades back up into a
//     bearish gap. Each zone is locked after it fires, so a setup is produced once per gap
//     instead of repeating on every bar price spends inside it.
//
//  4) COMPLETE TRADE FRAMEWORK
//     Entry is taken at the near edge of the gap, or at its 50% equilibrium if selected.
//     Invalidation is placed beyond the far edge plus an ATR buffer, so the stop sits outside
//     the zone rather than on its boundary. Initial risk is then measured and four targets are
//     projected as user-defined multiples of that risk.
//
//  5) UNIVERSAL SCALING
//     No pip values, point distances or price constants appear anywhere in the logic. Every
//     distance derives from ATR, from the gap's own height, or from risk multiples. The same
//     settings therefore behave correctly on Forex, Gold, indices, crypto, futures and equities,
//     from one-minute charts to monthly, with no code changes.
//
//  6) LIVE TRADE TRACKING
//     While a setup is unresolved its risk region, reward region, level lines, labels and
//     projection extend with price. The moment the final target or the stop is reached, the
//     whole setup freezes on the chart as a permanent record of how it resolved.
//
//  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
//  │  R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T                                                │
//  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//  Gap detection and tap confirmation are gated on confirmed bars, so a zone or a setup is never
//  created from an unfinished candle and never disappears afterwards. Entry, stop and all four
//  targets are fixed at the moment the setup is generated and never recalculated. The optional
//  higher-timeframe filter is requested with lookahead disabled.
//
//  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
//  │  D I S C L A I M E R                                                                    │
//  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute
//  financial advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. Use
//  proper risk management and consult a licensed financial advisor before trading real capital.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

indicator("FVG Trade Entries", "FVG TE", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  I N P U T S
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gFvg = "═════  FAIR VALUE GAP DETECTION  ═════"
showZones = input.bool(true,  "Show FVG Zones",              group = gFvg)
minMult   = input.float(0.10, "Min FVG Size (x ATR)",        minval = 0.0, maxval = 5, step = 0.05, group = gFvg, tooltip = "Gaps smaller than this multiple of ATR are ignored. Raise it to remove micro-imbalances on fast charts.")
atrLen    = input.int(14,     "ATR Length",                  minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = gFvg)
extendUn  = input.bool(true,  "Extend Zone Until Mitigated", group = gFvg)
extendBar = input.int(60,     "Zone Extension (bars)",       minval = 1, maxval = 500, group = gFvg, tooltip = "Used when 'Extend Until Mitigated' is off.")
maxZones  = input.int(20,     "Max Zones Tracked",           minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = gFvg)
delMitig  = input.bool(false, "Delete Zone Once Mitigated",  group = gFvg)
showFvgTx = input.bool(true,  "Show FVG Tag",                group = gFvg)

gFlt = "═════  SETUP FILTERS  ═════"
firstOnly = input.bool(true,  "Only First Tap Per Zone",     group = gFlt)
oneAtTime = input.bool(true,  "One Active Setup At A Time",  group = gFlt)
allowLong = input.bool(true,  "Allow Long Setups",           group = gFlt, inline = "dir")
allowShrt = input.bool(true,  "Allow Short Setups",          group = gFlt, inline = "dir")
useHtf    = input.bool(false, "Higher-Timeframe Trend Filter", group = gFlt)
htfTf     = input.timeframe("240", "Filter Timeframe",       group = gFlt)
htfEmaLen = input.int(50,     "Filter EMA Length",           minval = 2, maxval = 400, group = gFlt)

gTrd = "═════  ENTRY / STOP / TARGETS  ═════"
entryMode = input.string("Zone Edge", "Entry Mode", options = ["Zone Edge", "Zone Midpoint"], group = gTrd)
slBuffer  = input.float(0.30, "SL Buffer (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3, step = 0.05, group = gTrd)
rr1       = input.float(1.0,  "TP1 R:R", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = gTrd, inline = "r1")
rr2       = input.float(2.0,  "TP2 R:R", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = gTrd, inline = "r1")
rr3       = input.float(3.0,  "TP3 R:R", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = gTrd, inline = "r2")
rr4       = input.float(4.0,  "TP4 R:R", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = gTrd, inline = "r2")
maxTrades = input.int(5,      "Max Setups On Chart", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = gTrd)
tradeExt  = input.int(80,     "Setup Projection (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 500, group = gTrd, tooltip = "How far a resolved setup is drawn forward. A live setup keeps extending until it resolves.")

gVis = "═════  VISUALS  ═════"
showRisk  = input.bool(true, "Shade Risk Region",    group = gVis)
showRwd   = input.bool(true, "Shade Reward Region",  group = gVis)
showProj  = input.bool(true, "Show Projection Line", group = gVis)
showMidTp = input.bool(true, "Show TP1 / TP2 / TP3 Lines", group = gVis)
showLbls  = input.bool(true, "Show Level Labels",    group = gVis)
lblSize   = input.string("Small", "Label Size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gVis)

gSty = "═════  STYLE  ═════"
colBullZ  = input.color(color.new(#2962ff, 80), "Bullish FVG Zone", group = gSty, inline = "z")
colBearZ  = input.color(color.new(#ef5350, 80), "Bearish FVG Zone", group = gSty, inline = "z")
colRisk   = input.color(color.new(#ef5350, 72), "Risk Region",   group = gSty, inline = "rr")
colRwd    = input.color(color.new(#2962ff, 72), "Reward Region", group = gSty, inline = "rr")
colEntry  = input.color(#000000, "Entry Line",  group = gSty, inline = "ln")
colSl     = input.color(#000000, "Stop Line",   group = gSty, inline = "ln")
colTp     = input.color(#000000, "Target Line", group = gSty, inline = "ln")
colProj   = input.color(#2962ff, "Projection",  group = gSty)
colText   = input.color(#000000, "Label Text",  group = gSty)

string lblSz = lblSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : lblSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  T Y P E S
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
type Fvg
    box   zone
    label tag
    float top
    float bot
    bool  bull
    bool  used
    bool  dead
    int   born

type Setup
    box   riskB
    box   rwdB
    line  lnEntry
    line  lnSl
    line  lnT1
    line  lnT2
    line  lnT3
    line  lnT4
    line  proj
    label lbEntry
    label lbSl
    label lbT1
    label lbT2
    label lbT3
    label lbT4
    float entry
    float sl
    float t1
    float t2
    float t3
    float t4
    bool  bull
    bool  open
    int   startX

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  H E L P E R S
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
method erase(Fvg f) =>
    box.delete(f.zone)
    label.delete(f.tag)

method erase(Setup s) =>
    box.delete(s.riskB)
    box.delete(s.rwdB)
    line.delete(s.lnEntry)
    line.delete(s.lnSl)
    line.delete(s.lnT1)
    line.delete(s.lnT2)
    line.delete(s.lnT3)
    line.delete(s.lnT4)
    line.delete(s.proj)
    label.delete(s.lbEntry)
    label.delete(s.lbSl)
    label.delete(s.lbT1)
    label.delete(s.lbT2)
    label.delete(s.lbT3)
    label.delete(s.lbT4)

method stretch(Setup s, int x) =>
    if not na(s.riskB)
        box.set_right(s.riskB, x)
    if not na(s.rwdB)
        box.set_right(s.rwdB, x)
    if not na(s.lnEntry)
        line.set_x2(s.lnEntry, x)
    if not na(s.lnSl)
        line.set_x2(s.lnSl, x)
    if not na(s.lnT1)
        line.set_x2(s.lnT1, x)
    if not na(s.lnT2)
        line.set_x2(s.lnT2, x)
    if not na(s.lnT3)
        line.set_x2(s.lnT3, x)
    if not na(s.lnT4)
        line.set_x2(s.lnT4, x)
    if not na(s.proj)
        line.set_x2(s.proj, x)
    if not na(s.lbEntry)
        label.set_x(s.lbEntry, x)
    if not na(s.lbSl)
        label.set_x(s.lbSl, x)
    if not na(s.lbT1)
        label.set_x(s.lbT1, x)
    if not na(s.lbT2)
        label.set_x(s.lbT2, x)
    if not na(s.lbT3)
        label.set_x(s.lbT3, x)
    if not na(s.lbT4)
        label.set_x(s.lbT4, x)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  C O R E   S E R I E S
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
float atr    = ta.atr(atrLen)
float htfEma = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf, ta.ema(close, htfEmaLen), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
bool  htfUp  = not useHtf or (not na(htfEma) and close > htfEma)
bool  htfDn  = not useHtf or (not na(htfEma) and close < htfEma)

var array<Fvg>   zones  = array.new<Fvg>()
var array<Setup> setups = array.new<Setup>()

bool longSetup  = false
bool shortSetup = false

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  1)  F V G   D E T E C T I O N
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool rawBull = low > high[2]
bool rawBear = high < low[2]

if barstate.isconfirmed and not na(atr)
    float gTop = na
    float gBot = na
    bool  isB  = false
    bool  found = false

    if rawBull
        gBot  := high[2]
        gTop  := low
        isB   := true
        found := true
    else if rawBear
        gBot  := high
        gTop  := low[2]
        isB   := false
        found := true

    if found and (gTop - gBot) >= atr * minMult
        Fvg f = Fvg.new()
        f.top  := gTop
        f.bot  := gBot
        f.bull := isB
        f.used := false
        f.dead := false
        f.born := bar_index

        if showZones
            int rx = extendUn ? bar_index : bar_index + extendBar
            f.zone := box.new(bar_index - 2, gTop, rx, gBot, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 100), bgcolor = isB ? colBullZ : colBearZ)
            if showFvgTx
                f.tag := label.new(bar_index - 2, gBot, "FVG", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_none, textcolor = color.new(colText, 25), size = size.tiny)

        zones.push(f)

        while zones.size() > maxZones
            Fvg old = zones.shift()
            old.erase()

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  2)  Z O N E   M A I N T E N A N C E ,   M I T I G A T I O N   &   T A P   T R I G G E R
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool haveOpen = false
if setups.size() > 0
    for k = 0 to setups.size() - 1
        if setups.get(k).open
            haveOpen := true

if zones.size() > 0
    for i = zones.size() - 1 to 0
        Fvg f = zones.get(i)

        // keep an unmitigated zone extending to the right
        if extendUn and not f.dead and not na(f.zone)
            box.set_right(f.zone, bar_index)

        if barstate.isconfirmed and not f.dead
            // full mitigation: price has completely traded through the imbalance
            bool filled = f.bull ? close < f.bot : close > f.top
            if filled
                f.dead := true
                if delMitig
                    f.erase()
                    zones.remove(i)

            else
                // tap: price has re-entered the unfilled window
                bool reached = f.bull ? low <= f.top : high >= f.bot
                bool tapped   = reached and bar_index > f.born
                bool allowed = f.bull ? allowLong and htfUp : allowShrt and htfDn
                bool notLocked = not (firstOnly and f.used)
                bool slotFree = not (oneAtTime and haveOpen)

                if tapped and allowed and notLocked and slotFree
                    f.used := true

                    // ─── entry / stop / targets ───────────────────────────────────────────
                    float entry = f.bull ? (entryMode == "Zone Edge" ? f.top : (f.top + f.bot) / 2.0) : (entryMode == "Zone Edge" ? f.bot : (f.top + f.bot) / 2.0)
                    float stop  = f.bull ? f.bot - atr * slBuffer : f.top + atr * slBuffer
                    float risk  = math.abs(entry - stop)

                    if risk > 0
                        float d = f.bull ? 1.0 : -1.0
                        Setup s = Setup.new()
                        s.entry  := entry
                        s.sl     := stop
                        s.t1     := entry + d * risk * rr1
                        s.t2     := entry + d * risk * rr2
                        s.t3     := entry + d * risk * rr3
                        s.t4     := entry + d * risk * rr4
                        s.bull   := f.bull
                        s.open   := true
                        s.startX := math.max(0, f.born - 2)

                        int x1 = s.startX
                        int x2 = bar_index

                        if showRisk
                            s.riskB := box.new(x1, math.max(entry, stop), x2, math.min(entry, stop), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 100), bgcolor = colRisk)
                        if showRwd
                            s.rwdB := box.new(x1, math.max(entry, s.t4), x2, math.min(entry, s.t4), border_color = color.new(color.gray, 100), bgcolor = colRwd)

                        s.lnEntry := line.new(x1, entry, x2, entry, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = colEntry, width = 2)
                        s.lnSl    := line.new(x1, stop,  x2, stop,  xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = colSl,    width = 2)
                        s.lnT4    := line.new(x1, s.t4,  x2, s.t4,  xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = colTp,    width = 2)
                        if showMidTp
                            s.lnT1 := line.new(x1, s.t1, x2, s.t1, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colTp, 45), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
                            s.lnT2 := line.new(x1, s.t2, x2, s.t2, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colTp, 45), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
                            s.lnT3 := line.new(x1, s.t3, x2, s.t3, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colTp, 45), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
                        if showProj
                            s.proj := line.new(x1, entry, x2, s.t4, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = colProj, style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)

                        if showLbls
                            s.lbEntry := label.new(x2, entry, "ENTRY",        xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor = colText, size = lblSz)
                            s.lbSl    := label.new(x2, stop,  "STOP LOSS",    xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor = colText, size = lblSz)
                            s.lbT4    := label.new(x2, s.t4,  "FINAL TARGET", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor = colText, size = lblSz)
                            if showMidTp
                                s.lbT1 := label.new(x2, s.t1, "TP1", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor = color.new(colText, 25), size = size.tiny)
                                s.lbT2 := label.new(x2, s.t2, "TP2", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor = color.new(colText, 25), size = size.tiny)
                                s.lbT3 := label.new(x2, s.t3, "TP3", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor = color.new(colText, 25), size = size.tiny)

                        setups.push(s)
                        haveOpen := true

                        if f.bull
                            longSetup := true
                        else
                            shortSetup := true

                        while setups.size() > maxTrades
                            Setup oldS = setups.shift()
                            oldS.erase()

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  3)  L I V E   S E T U P   T R A C K I N G
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool tpHit = false
bool slHit = false

if setups.size() > 0
    for j = 0 to setups.size() - 1
        Setup s = setups.get(j)
        if s.open
            s.stretch(bar_index)

            if barstate.isconfirmed
                bool hitSl = s.bull ? low  <= s.sl : high >= s.sl
                bool hitT4 = s.bull ? high >= s.t4 : low  <= s.t4
                bool hitT1 = s.bull ? high >= s.t1 : low  <= s.t1

                if hitT1
                    tpHit := true
                if hitSl
                    slHit := true
                    s.open := false
                    s.stretch(bar_index)
                else if hitT4
                    s.open := false
                    s.stretch(bar_index + 2)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  4)  A L E R T S
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
alertcondition(longSetup,  "Bullish FVG Tap – Long Setup",  "FVG Trade Entries: price tapped an unmitigated bullish Fair Value Gap on {{ticker}} {{interval}} — long setup generated.")
alertcondition(shortSetup, "Bearish FVG Tap – Short Setup", "FVG Trade Entries: price tapped an unmitigated bearish Fair Value Gap on {{ticker}} {{interval}} — short setup generated.")
alertcondition(tpHit,      "Target Reached",                "FVG Trade Entries: an active setup reached its first target on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(slHit,      "Stop Loss Reached",             "FVG Trade Entries: an active setup was invalidated on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if longSetup
    alert("FVG Long Setup — " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if shortSetup
    alert("FVG Short Setup — " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  5)  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plot(atr,                  "ATR",              color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(zones.size(),         "Zones Tracked",    color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(haveOpen ? 1 : 0,     "Setup Active",     color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)